  <h3>Start a Worker with one command</h3>
  <p class="muted">Run this on the machine that should become a Worker. The key is visible in the process list while the command runs; use the file variant below on shared machines.</p>
  <pre id="invite-oneliner">minion worker up --server https://hub.example.com --invite-key mnk_9f2c1ab7.m5xwy3dpnz2g65tfobqxgzljnrswc43foj2xizlsmvzwk5dm</pre>
  <button type="button" data-copy="#invite-oneliner">Copy the command</button>
  <h3>Same, with the key in a file</h3>
  <pre id="invite-file">(
  umask 077 &amp;&amp;
  dir=$(mktemp -d &#34;${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/minion-invite.XXXXXX&#34;) &amp;&amp;
  trap &#39;rm -rf &#34;$dir&#34;&#39; EXIT &amp;&amp;
  cat &gt; &#34;$dir/invite.key&#34; &lt;&lt;&#39;EOF&#39; &amp;&amp;
mnk_9f2c1ab7.m5xwy3dpnz2g65tfobqxgzljnrswc43foj2xizlsmvzwk5dm
EOF
  minion worker up --server https://hub.example.com --invite-key &#34;$dir/invite.key&#34;
)
</pre>
  <button type="button" data-copy="#invite-file">Copy the commands</button>
  <h3>Docker Compose</h3>
  <p class="muted">A complete Compose project that needs only Docker, <code>bootstrap.sh</code> from the release and the key in a file. The key stays in a secret file; the container reads it through <code>MINION_INVITE_KEY_FILE</code>.</p>
  <pre id="invite-compose"># A Minion Worker in Docker, started from the invitation key. Before you start:
# 1. Put bootstrap.sh next to this file. It is a file of the Minion release:
#    https://github.com/patrick-1984/ai-minion/releases/latest/download/bootstrap.sh
# 2. Save the key as the only line of invite_key.txt next to this file.
# 3. Run: docker compose up -d
# 4. Approve the new Worker in the Hub (Workers page): it starts pending and gets no operations until you do.
# The image is built from Alpine with tmux (the Worker drives its sessions through tmux);
# bootstrap.sh downloads and verifies the minion binary on the first start and keeps it in
# the cache volume. The Worker runs as user 10001:10001 and enrolls once: after that the key
# is not needed, but KEEP the file invite_key.txt: Docker needs the mounted file to exist
# whenever the container is restarted or recreated, and the Worker reads it on every start.
# An empty file is safe (an enrolled Worker ignores the key), a missing one stops the start.
# After enrollment erase the secret in place. The init service made the file belong to user
# 10001:10001 (mode 600), so your own shell may not write to it; let the root init service do it:
#    docker compose run --rm --no-deps init sh -c &#39;: &gt; /invite_key.txt&#39;
# That truncates the same file (do not delete, move or replace it with an editor). To remove
# the file itself instead, first remove invite_key.txt from init&#39;s volumes, the secret and
# MINION_INVITE_KEY_FILE, then run: docker compose up -d --remove-orphans
services:
  init:
    image: alpine:3.22
    user: &#34;0:0&#34;
    command: [&#34;sh&#34;, &#34;-c&#34;, &#34;chown -R 10001:10001 /data /cache &amp;&amp; chown 10001:10001 /invite_key.txt &amp;&amp; chmod 600 /invite_key.txt&#34;]
    volumes:
      - ./worker-data:/data
      - minion-cache:/cache
      - ./invite_key.txt:/invite_key.txt
  minion-worker:
    build:
      context: .
      dockerfile_inline: |
        FROM alpine:3.22
        RUN apk add --no-cache tmux
    user: &#34;10001:10001&#34;
    depends_on:
      init:
        condition: service_completed_successfully
    restart: unless-stopped
    entrypoint: [&#34;/bin/sh&#34;, &#34;/bootstrap.sh&#34;]
    command: [&#34;worker&#34;, &#34;up&#34;]
    environment:
      MINION_SERVER: &#34;https://hub.example.com&#34;
      MINION_VERSION: ${MINION_VERSION:-latest}
      MINION_CACHE_DIR: /cache
      MINION_STATE_DIR: /data
      MINION_INVITE_KEY_FILE: /run/secrets/minion_invite_key
    volumes:
      - ./bootstrap.sh:/bootstrap.sh:ro
      - ./worker-data:/data
      - minion-cache:/cache
    secrets:
      - minion_invite_key
secrets:
  minion_invite_key:
    file: ./invite_key.txt
volumes:
  minion-cache:
</pre>
  <button type="button" data-copy="#invite-compose">Copy the Compose file</button>
  <p><a href="/invitations">Back to the invitation keys</a></p>
</div>